<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil up, meal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil up, meal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices rose by 50-100 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 3,000 tonnes compared to around 15,000 tonnes at the same time last year. Business was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices rose by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in local markets. Business volume were limited and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $288-289 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $116 for ready shipment and was $112 for March shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,900 rupees for ready delivery and was 3,750 rupees for March delivery in FOR (Free On Rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
